+// check in onBlur below can never see the button as the new focus target,
+// so onBlur ran commitTyped + isOpen=false immediately, unmounting the
+// panel before mouseup, so the click on the option never fired at all
+// (confirmed with Playwright webkit: pointerdown/mousedown land on the
+// button, mouseup lands back on the trigger input, no click event ever
+// dispatched). suppressBlurClose is a second, focus-independent signal set
+// on pointerdown anywhere in the panel (capture phase, so it runs before
+// blur) and cleared on the next global pointerup (after the browser has
+// already dispatched click, if any) -- it keeps the panel mounted long
+// enough for the option's own click handler to run in every browser.
+const suppressBlurClose = ref(false)
